    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d68">

                <pb facs="0065" n="55" sameAs="frus:frus1949v08/pg55"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.00/1–1849: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Consul General at Peiping</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Clubb</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Peiping</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1949-01-18T18:00:00+08:00">January 18, 1949—6
                            p. m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received 8:29 p. m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>61. Re Contel 54, January 18.<anchor n="6" xml:id="d68-f1"/> I am reliably
                    informed peace delegation comprising 11 persons including ex-mayor Ho Ssu-yuan
                    departed on mission from Peiping 3:30 p. m. today.</p>
                <p>Information received by USIS director about same time was that General Fu Tso-yi
                    had dispatched his own delegate one-half hour previously.</p>
                <p>Sent Department 61, repeated Nanking 57, Shanghai 57.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Clubb</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
